abstract: >-
  Research software accompanying Part I of a comparative study of
  traditional and explainable machine-learning approaches to credit risk
  modeling using the OpenIntro Loans Full Schema dataset. The framework
  compares Logistic Regression, Random Forest, XGBoost, and LightGBM, with
  training-partition SMOTE, SHAP explanations, exploratory threshold
  selection, and preliminary income-group fairness checks.

keywords:
  - credit risk
  - machine learning
  - explainable AI
  - XAI
  - SHAP
  - LightGBM
  - SMOTE
  - fair lending
  - data science
  - python

